/-- **The multi-hub `Hdom` reduces to the single-hub tie bound.**  With `pairCollapse6` a theorem,
    every nonempty Balanced+Capped state (ANY length, stuck or not) is `Aobj`-dominated by the tie
    at its own size, PROVIDED the single-hub slice holds -- i.e. the entire `m >= 3` obligation is
    discharged modulo the (single-hub) tie-definition layer.  This unifies the multi-hub and
    single-hub residuals into one: the non-aligned-n `tie : ℕ → UTree` representative bound. -/
theorem hdom_of_singleHubDom (tie : ℕ → UTree)
    (hsingle : ∀ h : Hub, Balanced [h] → Capped [h] →
        Aobj (backboneU [h]) ≤ Aobj (tie (stateSize [h]))) :
    ∀ s : List Hub, Balanced s → Capped s → s ≠ [] →
      Aobj (backboneU s) ≤ Aobj (tie (stateSize s)) :=
  hdom_of_pairCollapse6_and_singleHubDom pairCollapse6 tie hsingle

